      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "David Wake",
      "description": "Scalpay Fish Processing Factory -now closed. The 2880 sq. m plant, operational from March 2001 to early 2005, was constructed by Highlands and Islands Enterprise and was being rented by Stolt Sea Farms on a 20 yr lease. The £10m development is expected to provide 109 full time equivalent jobs, with investment of £4.5m by HIE. Following a merger of Stolt the factory was closed after only 4 years. Fish is now processed on the mainland. There is hope that the factory will re-open for the processing of mussels, should the proposed farm on Taransay go ahead.",
      "dateCreated": "2006-03-03",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "scalpay-outer-hebrides-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gf73",
      "smallPath": "_m/g/f/7/3/scalpay-outer-hebrides-wp/scalpay-fish-processing-factor-small.webp"
    },
